  "caveat": "Software-rendered WebGL (SwiftShader) on a shared 4-CPU container with no GPU, under heavy load from other jobs. Long tasks are attributed from the trace (longTaskAnatomy and longTaskCauses): with SwiftShader the GPU process composites and rasterizes on the CPU, so synchronous WebGL calls (context creation, the first use of a shader program) can wait behind a slow SwapBuffers. Frame intervals and absolute times understate real hardware and never prove smoothness. JavaScript self time by owner (CPU profile), render submission per frame, renderer counts and heap are the closest hardware-independent signals. Long tasks come from the page's longtask observer; selfTimeMs.browserNative is native browser work outside JavaScript (with software WebGL this includes waiting on the rasterizing GPU process), so a long task without matching JavaScript self time is not script work. scriptPerFrameMs buckets top-level script events between frame starts and overstates the tail when frames are sparse. Real-GPU and device smoothness must be confirmed by a person on that hardware.",
  "notes": {
    "programs": "Linked shader programs come from the stand-in's extra programs field; the contract's stats do not include programs yet.",
    "renderSubmissionMs": "Main-thread time inside each renderer.render call over the most recent rendered frames (up to 120), from the stand-in's extra submissionTimesMs field.",
    "framePacingMs": "The contract's frameTimesMs as the stand-in fills it: intervals between rendered frames during continuous rendering (a definition requested for the contract), so GPU-bound frames count. Adaptive quality reads it.",
    "longTaskAnatomy": "Per long task: wall time, the renderer main thread's own CPU time (threadMs), time inside script events, time blocked on GPU-process round trips (gpuWaitMs: CommandBufferProxyImpl::WaitFor* slices), how long the GPU process main thread was busy meanwhile and with what (gpuProcessTop). cause classifies the task: waiting on the GPU process, renderer thread off-CPU (host contention: wall time far above thread time without GPU waits), or renderer main-thread work."
  }
